& [Formation] means signed prospective constraints
  + formation describes a protocol shape that a later implementation authority may adopt
  + formation is not implementation, executable availability, execution, observation, or proof
  + formation can be superseded only by explicit lineage and signature

& [ScannerProfile] means observation-policy identity
  + scanner profile 0.1 identifies no-follow traversal and scanner policy
  + it does not identify topology receipt JSON schema
  + it does not prove an executable exists
  + current forms and receipt profiles identify their own representation meanings

& [Observation] means one bounded producer result
  + observation is an output of a separately authorized physical operation
  + pure caller-supplied data is not observation
  + a form saying observed does not establish the event occurred

& [ActualAcquisition] means an authorized physical producer event
  + actual distinguishes performed observation from representable data
  + acquisition has stable identity, producer lineage, scope, start, completion, and result
  + this formation revision names required relations but performs no acquisition

& [CompleteAcquisition] means closure under one exact contract
  + complete is relative to the full scanner traversal, policy, and resource rules
  + successful structural assembly of supplied values is not physical enumeration completeness
  + completion failure produces no evidence-grade acquisition

& [Repeated] means two distinct actual events
  + two references to one event are not repetition
  + two copies of one carrier are not repetition
  + two caller-supplied carriers are not repetition
  + repetition requires distinct acquisition identities and exact order

& [First] and [Second] are causal roles
  + first completes before second starts
  + roles are established by an order edge, not names or operand positions
  + left and right reconciliation operands remain positional and non-temporal
  + the abstract order edge does not select wall clock, monotonic clock, or timestamp fields

& [Lineage] means retained derivation ancestry
  + acquisition lineage identifies producer, event, scope, completion, inventory, digest carrier, and relations
  + lineage is not replaced by a digest alone
  + independent means neither acquisition lineage is a mutable alias of the other

& [CommonScope] means equality of every semantic scope coordinate
  + candidate root reference, root identity, and volume path
  + scanner, forms, encoding, limits, and policy identities
  + predecessor admission identity and comparison scope
  + omission is not wildcard equality

& [Equal] means canonical committed subjects compare exactly
  + current reconciliation rederives each carrier before comparing
  + Equal is one required derivation edge
  + Equal does not prove actual acquisition, repetition, order, or present state

& [NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual] means the complete conjunction
  + two distinct actual complete acquisitions
  + exact first-complete-before-second-start order
  + exact common scope
  + independent complete canonical carrier lineage
  + current reconciliation disposition Equal
  + no stronger state claim

& [NonAtomic] is a mandatory denial
  + no snapshot, transaction, lock, indivisible walk, or uninterrupted unchanged interval
  + no exclusion of change-and-restore
  + no exclusion of later change
  + no exclusion of external writers

& [EvidenceConstruction] means deriving a supported grade
  + evidence construction consumes proof edges under future authority
  + enum construction is not evidence construction
  + receipt construction is not evidence construction
  + pure reconciliation alone is not evidence construction

& [ReceiptFormValidity] means pure coherence
  + exact current profiles and fields decode
  + all internal relations validate
  + validity permits representing a claimed grade
  + validity does not prove derivation or issuer authority

& [ReceiptIssuance] means an authority-bearing claim act
  + issuer binds evidence derivation to exact receipt subject and fields
  + issuer identity and authority are separately required
  + no current public validator, serializer, or SJS processor is an issuer

& [Consumption] means later stateful acceptance control
  + validates issuer, lineage, freshness, scope, and single use
  + consumption is distinct from decoding and issuance
  + consumption is absent from this revision

& [WorldState] means conditions outside exact evidence boundaries
  + present unchanged state is unknown
  + uninterrupted stability is unknown
  + external-writer absence is unknown
  + physical immutability is unknown
  + evidence must not be linguistically inflated into these claims

& [LegacyFormation] means preserved historical authority
  + old vocabulary accurately records the earlier formation
  + it is not current governing meaning after explicit replacement signature
  + history is preserved rather than decoded or rewritten

& [ClauseRefinement_SameScope] is complete equality
  + same never means selected subset or best effort
  + all declared dimensions must be present and equal

& [ClauseRefinement_ImmediatelyBeforeIssuance] is not freshness proof
  + physical proximity is not defined by prose alone
  + later issuer contract must bind exact order and freshness evidence
  + no current clock or interval is activated

& [ClauseRefinement_IndependentlyComplete] applies twice
  + first acquisition cannot borrow missing completeness from second
  + second acquisition cannot borrow missing completeness from first
  + reconciliation cannot repair incomplete inputs

& [ClauseRefinement_SubordinateEqual] prevents promotion
  + Equal is necessary but insufficient
  + acquisition, order, and scope edges are independently mandatory
  + no conversion function may manufacture the grade from reconciliation output alone

& [InferenceRules] are closed
  + two distinct actual complete acquisitions plus exact causal order plus exact common scope plus independent complete carrier lineage plus current Equal reconciliation may support NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual under future issuer authority
  + receipt-form validity may support only a claim that the representation is coherent
  + replacement formation signature may support only current prospective governance

& [AntiInferenceRules] are mandatory
  - never: infer formation implies implementation
  - never: infer scanner profile implies executable availability
  - never: infer supplied means observed
  - never: infer complete structural carrier means complete physical enumeration
  - never: infer repeated from two references or values
  - never: infer first and second from left and right
  - never: infer actual acquisition from Equal
  - never: infer issuer authority from valid receipt
  - never: infer consumption from issuance
  - never: infer quiescence, snapshot, stability, immutability, or current truth from non-atomic repeated equality

& [VocabularyDisposition] is exact
  + accept formation_reconciliation
  + accept InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + accept NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + accept non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + accept consistency_evidence
  + accept actual_acquisition only as later authority-bearing event
  + accept first and second only as causal acquisition roles
  + reserve quiescent, stable, unchanged, snapshot, immutable, safe, issued, and consumed unless their separate contracts are proven
  + reject quiescent_double_inventory and consistency as current scanner formation vocabulary

& [RefinementDecision] is passed
  + no source correction required
  + abstract causal order avoids premature clock design
  + scanner observation policy and receipt representation identities remain distinct
  + every ambiguous term has one selected meaning or explicit reservation
  + constraint extraction and reapplication remain next
  + implementation authority is absent
  + execution authority is absent
  + physical authority is absent
